WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:02.523
- Good Morning, Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.523 --> 00:00:05.547
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:08.298
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:08.298 --> 00:00:09.375
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:12.724
today's message is fall forward.

00:00:12.724 --> 00:00:14.814
Over to you, Denzel Washington.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.205
(rooster crows)

00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:19.696
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:19.696 --> 00:00:22.517
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:26.412
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:29.115
- I've found that nothing in life

00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:32.115
is worthwhile unless you take risks.

00:00:33.112 --> 00:00:33.945
Nothing.

00:00:35.198 --> 00:00:39.047
Nelson Mandela said, "There
is no passion to be found

00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:42.258
"playing small and
settling for a life that's

00:00:42.258 --> 00:00:46.135
"less than the one you're
capable of living."

00:00:46.135 --> 00:00:48.160
Now, I'm sure in your
experiences in school

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.588
and applying to college
and picking your major

00:00:50.588 --> 00:00:52.625
and deciding what you
want to do with life,

00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:54.875
I'm sure people have told you to make sure

00:00:54.875 --> 00:00:56.750
you have something to fall back on,

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.383
make sure you got something
to fall back on, honey.

00:01:00.383 --> 00:01:02.807
But I never understood that concept,

00:01:02.807 --> 00:01:05.875
having something to fall back on.

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:08.333
If I'm going to fall,

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:11.721
I don't want to fall back on anything

00:01:11.721 --> 00:01:13.638
except my faith.

00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:16.050
I want to fall forward.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.217
I figure at least this way
I'll see what I'm going to hit.

00:01:21.278 --> 00:01:22.361
Fall forward.

00:01:23.422 --> 00:01:25.089
This is what I mean.

00:01:26.154 --> 00:01:29.031
Reggie Jackson struck out
2,600 times in his career,

00:01:29.031 --> 00:01:31.775
the most in the history of baseball,

00:01:31.775 --> 00:01:33.489
but you don't hear about the strike outs.

00:01:33.489 --> 00:01:35.989
People remember the home runs.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.163
Fall forward.

00:01:39.695 --> 00:01:42.945
Thomas Edison conducted
1,000 failed experiments.

00:01:42.945 --> 00:01:45.377
Did you know that? I didn't know that.

00:01:45.377 --> 00:01:49.544
Because the one thousand and
first was the light bulb.

00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:51.950
Fall forward.

00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:57.182
Every failed experiment is
one step closer to success.

00:01:57.182 --> 00:01:59.156
- So I love the concept of falling forward

00:01:59.156 --> 00:02:01.384
and seeing failures not as true failures

00:02:01.384 --> 00:02:04.310
but as opportunities to learn
and grow and get better.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.835
I think it also applies
to how we see ourselves

00:02:06.835 --> 00:02:08.924
in our daily lives and
the decisions we make

00:02:08.924 --> 00:02:10.742
and how hard we are on ourselves.

00:02:10.742 --> 00:02:13.129
I believe that you need
to kick yourself forward

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:14.881
instead of kicking yourself down.

00:02:14.881 --> 00:02:16.790
I once got asked in an interview

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:18.272
by the reporter who was saying,

00:02:18.272 --> 00:02:21.074
"How hard should you be on yourself?

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.041
"Can you be too hard on yourself?"

00:02:23.041 --> 00:02:24.825
And at first I was
confused by the question.

00:02:24.825 --> 00:02:26.636
Too hard on yourself, how can
you be too hard on yourself?

00:02:26.636 --> 00:02:28.524
No, you can't be too hard on yourself.

00:02:28.524 --> 00:02:30.585
And after going home
and thinking about it,

00:02:30.585 --> 00:02:33.392
I was actually frustrated with my answer

00:02:33.392 --> 00:02:36.801
because I'm so in on the
hard on myself forward

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.482
and kicking myself forward
that the part that I missed

00:02:39.482 --> 00:02:41.896
was most people kick themselves down.

00:02:41.896 --> 00:02:44.325
Most people are so hard on themselves

00:02:44.325 --> 00:02:46.059
that then they don't take any action,

00:02:46.059 --> 00:02:47.704
that they tell themselves
they can't do something,

00:02:47.704 --> 00:02:49.898
that they suck and they'll
never amount to anything,

00:02:49.898 --> 00:02:51.707
and they have no value,
and they should quit

00:02:51.707 --> 00:02:52.928
and go off and do something else.

00:02:52.928 --> 00:02:54.899
Those people just kick themselves down,

00:02:54.899 --> 00:02:58.274
where what you want is the
ability to kick yourself forward,

00:02:58.274 --> 00:03:01.926
to say, "This sucked,
I know I can do better.

00:03:01.926 --> 00:03:04.815
"What I just created is not my best work.

00:03:04.815 --> 00:03:07.928
"Here are the 20 areas
that I need to improve on,

00:03:07.928 --> 00:03:09.981
"and I'm going to go and
work on that right now."

00:03:09.981 --> 00:03:13.616
To see the failure and the
negativity and the holes

00:03:13.616 --> 00:03:15.759
in what you're making and use that

00:03:15.759 --> 00:03:17.894
as motivation to go off and do better.

00:03:17.894 --> 00:03:20.109
That's how I default to, I think it's how

00:03:20.109 --> 00:03:23.152
most entrepreneurs will default
to, you kind of have to.

00:03:23.152 --> 00:03:25.944
If you just live in negativity land

00:03:25.944 --> 00:03:27.436
of how much you suck and
how you're never going to

00:03:27.436 --> 00:03:29.517
get anywhere, you're just
kicking yourself down,

00:03:29.517 --> 00:03:31.671
it's really hard to build
a successful business.

00:03:31.671 --> 00:03:32.972
If you are that hard on yourself

00:03:32.972 --> 00:03:34.796
and you never take any action,

00:03:34.796 --> 00:03:36.201
you're never going to get anywhere.

00:03:36.201 --> 00:03:38.406
But entrepreneurs who
are hard on themselves,

00:03:38.406 --> 00:03:40.479
that kick themselves forward,

00:03:40.479 --> 00:03:41.722
they could be harder on themselves

00:03:41.722 --> 00:03:43.213
than anybody else around them

00:03:43.213 --> 00:03:46.457
but in a positive way that
pushes them to action,

00:03:46.457 --> 00:03:48.061
those are the people who win.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.242
So, I encourage you to think about

00:03:50.242 --> 00:03:52.693
you being hard on yourself.

00:03:52.693 --> 00:03:54.839
Is it helping you?

00:03:54.839 --> 00:03:56.710
Are you just beating yourself up

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:58.330
or are you using it as motivation

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.652
and fuel to do a better job?

00:04:00.652 --> 00:04:02.707
So I'm going to make that
the question of the day.

00:04:02.707 --> 00:04:05.537
Question of the day: Do
you kick yourself down,

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:07.563
or do you kick yourself forward?

00:04:07.563 --> 00:04:09.932
Super curious, leave it
in the comments below.

00:04:09.932 --> 00:04:10.872
I also want to give a quick shout out

00:04:10.872 --> 00:04:12.490
to Jean from 3rdeye Brand.

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:13.843
Jean, thank you so much for picking up

00:04:13.843 --> 00:04:15.706
a copy of my book, Your One Word,

00:04:15.706 --> 00:04:17.454
and posting that picture on Instagram.

00:04:17.454 --> 00:04:18.981
I really, really, really appreciate it,

00:04:18.981 --> 00:04:20.603
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:20.603 --> 00:04:21.962
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:21.962 --> 00:04:24.376
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:04:24.376 --> 00:04:27.282
in yourself and whatever your one word is.

00:04:27.282 --> 00:04:29.775
Much love, and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:04:29.775 --> 00:04:32.472
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:34.923
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:04:34.923 --> 00:04:38.703
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:04:38.703 --> 00:04:41.301
(keys typing)

00:04:41.301 --> 00:04:43.077
- And as you begin to challenge yourself,

00:04:43.077 --> 00:04:44.984
you'll discover some things about yourself

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.726
that you don't know right now.

00:04:46.726 --> 00:04:48.760
The other thing is you
begin to look at yourself,

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.883
look at your dreams and
begin again to experiment

00:04:51.883 --> 00:04:54.211
and stepping into your greatness.

00:04:54.211 --> 00:04:55.841
One of the things that's very important,

00:04:55.841 --> 00:04:57.885
whatever goals and dreams that you have,

00:04:57.885 --> 00:05:01.422
repeat after me please: Make
your move before you're ready.

00:05:01.422 --> 00:05:03.430
- [Audience] Make your
move before you're ready.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.125
Yeah, Price Pritchett, who's
a great great motivator

00:05:06.125 --> 00:05:09.253
and trainer, he said, "Make
your move before you're ready."

00:05:09.253 --> 00:05:13.723
We're instructed in life to
walk by faith and not by sight.

00:05:13.723 --> 00:05:16.405
See, you want to really
begin to stretch yourself.

00:05:16.405 --> 00:05:17.904
You want to become a risk taker.

00:05:17.904 --> 00:05:20.119
You want to raise the bar on yourself.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.763
Most people won't do that.

00:05:21.763 --> 00:05:25.930
See, most people engage in
low-life living, low-risk living.

00:05:26.998 --> 00:05:29.066
This God said, "If you're
not willing to risk,

00:05:29.066 --> 00:05:31.376
"you cannot grow, and if you cannot grow,

00:05:31.376 --> 00:05:33.071
"you cannot become your best,

00:05:33.071 --> 00:05:36.846
"and if you cannot become
your best, you can't be happy,

00:05:36.846 --> 00:05:41.314
"and if you can't be happy,
then what else is there?"

00:05:41.314 --> 00:05:42.453
I like what Helen Keller said,

00:05:42.453 --> 00:05:46.276
"Life is short and unpredictable,
eat the dessert first."

00:05:46.276 --> 00:05:48.339
(audience laughing)

00:05:48.339 --> 00:05:50.464
And so you want to begin
to take some chances.

00:05:50.464 --> 00:05:52.287
You want to begin to challenge yourself

00:05:52.287 --> 00:05:55.548
and make it okay to fail and
learn from your failures.

00:05:55.548 --> 00:05:56.465
Don't allow

00:05:57.332 --> 00:05:58.600
fear

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:00.023
of failure

00:06:00.023 --> 00:06:02.856
and the allure, the attractiveness,

00:06:02.856 --> 00:06:06.474
of playing it safe in life to draw you in.

00:06:06.474 --> 00:06:07.905
You can't get out of life alive,

00:06:07.905 --> 00:06:10.325
you got to die to leave here.

00:06:10.325 --> 00:06:12.387
- The movies that I
made while I was making

00:06:12.387 --> 00:06:16.195
The Fresh Prince, so it
was The Fresh Prince during

00:06:16.195 --> 00:06:20.578
the winter, and then the
summers were Bad Boys,

00:06:20.578 --> 00:06:23.596
Independence Day, Men in Black, you know.

00:06:23.596 --> 00:06:26.013
So it really captured a time.

00:06:27.321 --> 00:06:29.654
So it's very difficult.

00:06:29.654 --> 00:06:32.612
I wouldn't have it any other way, I love

00:06:32.612 --> 00:06:36.779
being able to make people
smile and cheer over that,

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:42.314
but I also am going to
boldly go to new creation.

00:06:43.228 --> 00:06:45.978
Even something like the decision,

00:06:48.157 --> 00:06:50.738
I had the two screen plays in front of me

00:06:50.738 --> 00:06:55.150
for the Independence Day
2, and for Suicide Squad,

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.436
so I had to choose
between the two of those.

00:06:57.436 --> 00:07:00.858
And even the choice of
going to Suicide Squad,

00:07:00.858 --> 00:07:03.196
nothing about the qualities of the movies,

00:07:03.196 --> 00:07:06.425
but the choice of trying to go forward

00:07:06.425 --> 00:07:09.592
versus clinging and clawing backwards.

00:07:10.686 --> 00:07:13.084
I do want to aggressively go forward

00:07:13.084 --> 00:07:16.723
and do new things and
create, and hopefully

00:07:16.723 --> 00:07:19.550
be able to stumble upon a new heyday.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:22.134
- Failure is a part of the
learning process, right?

00:07:22.134 --> 00:07:23.926
What's the risk of failure?

00:07:23.926 --> 00:07:26.423
What, you'll be embarrassed
or risk of failure?

00:07:26.423 --> 00:07:27.955
How do you distinguish failure

00:07:27.955 --> 00:07:30.705
from learning in your whole life?

00:07:31.819 --> 00:07:34.850
Failure implies that it's
stopped, that the game stops.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:39.083
If it's part of your
failing and then you learn,

00:07:39.083 --> 00:07:43.611
then that learning is part
of the moving forward, right?

00:07:43.611 --> 00:07:45.742
So that is what the process is like:

00:07:45.742 --> 00:07:47.909
fail, learn, move forward.

00:07:48.998 --> 00:07:52.807
And constantly do that,
because you're cutting edge,

00:07:52.807 --> 00:07:54.729
you're going where people
haven't been before,

00:07:54.729 --> 00:07:56.911
and inventiveness, that's exciting.

